1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,333
Larry [unspoken model note]: I want to make a portrait of the cornet player after the ceremony.

2
00:00:06,753 --> 00:00:12,120
Larry: Rita, I'm rolling on the bandstand—this is all we've got for the seven, so make it count.

3
00:00:13,170 --> 00:00:16,956
Rita: Phil, you're live—go ahead and hit the groundhog numbers for us.

4
00:00:17,583 --> 00:00:22,042
Phil [unspoken model note]: The couch move is Wednesday, I have time.

5
00:00:22,462 --> 00:00:34,936
Phil: Rita, I'm heading out—coach is going in a minute. I'll sort the van stuff from Pittsburgh. Thanks for the week, love. Bye, Larry, if you're still around.

6
00:00:36,003 --> 00:00:54,974
Phil: Hey, it's Phil. I'm in Pittsburgh now, just off the coach. Listen, about tomorrow—van's booked for the couch, right? I want to nail down the pickup time and make sure I know which hallway we're dragging it through. I'll be at your place by noon, tops.

7
00:00:59,125 --> 00:01:03,167
Phil [unspoken model note]: It's Wednesday, February 3, 2016, 6:00 am.

8
00:01:03,587 --> 00:01:17,356
Phil: Morning, Rita. I'm out today—couch heave in Pittsburgh, one o'clock coach to get me there. You all locked for the seven, or do you want me to do a quick phone return before I vanish?

9
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:24,333
Phil [unspoken model note]: Wait, but looking at the remembered experiences, there are multiple "runs" or scenarios.

10
00:01:24,753 --> 00:01:29,666
Phil: Right, couch-hauling season. See you in the city, folks.
